---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "@/components/layout/PageHero.astro";
import ProductCTA from "@/components/products/ProductCTA.astro";
import ProductCover from "@/components/products/ProductCover.astro";
import FAQList from "@/components/ui/FAQList.astro";
import heroImage from "@/assets/brand/neutral-hero.png";
import { resolveProductCommerce } from "@/lib/lemon-squeezy";

const products = await getCollection("products");
const product = products.find((item) => item.data.slug === "developer-marketing-quickstart");
if (!product) throw new Error("Developer Marketing Quickstart product entry was not found.");
const d = product.data;
const commerce = resolveProductCommerce(d);

const steps = [
  ["Choose a buyer", "Pick an identifiable market you can investigate rather than declaring a permanent niche before you have evidence."],
  ["Investigate a problem", "Separate what you can observe from what you are inferring, then find a problem strong enough to justify a first test."],
  ["Shape a provisional offer", "Turn the problem into a bounded first offer with enough economic and delivery logic to be worth testing."],
  ["Choose one channel", "Pick a practical route for reaching the market instead of trying to operate every acquisition tactic at once."],
  ["Qualify a First 25", "Build a small prospect set where you can explain why each business deserves attention and who is likely to care."],
  ["Work the cycle", "Make contact, follow up where justified, stop where appropriate, and keep enough state to learn from what happened."],
  ["Choose the next test", "Use buyer response and operating evidence to change one meaningful part of the loop instead of replacing the whole strategy."],
];

const faqs = [
  { data: { order: 1, question: "Is the Quickstart a complete product?", answer: "Yes. It is a free first acquisition system designed to get one real loop into motion. The paid products go substantially deeper into marketing, acquisition operations, pricing, sales, and the rest of the freelance business." } },
  { data: { order: 2, question: "Do I need another Developer Business Lab product first?", answer: "No. The Quickstart is designed to stand on its own as a first move." } },
  { data: { order: 3, question: "What is the difference between this and Client Acquisition Without Upwork?", answer: "The Quickstart helps you activate one first acquisition loop. Client Acquisition Without Upwork is the deeper operating backbone for account selection, research, outreach, nurture, qualification, pipeline states, measurement, economics, capacity, and diagnosis." } },
  { data: { order: 4, question: "What is the difference between this and Marketing for Builders?", answer: "Marketing for Builders goes deeper into market understanding, positioning, proof, buyer-facing infrastructure, access routes, activation, and marketing management. The Quickstart is narrower and built around getting one acquisition cycle moving." } },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Developer Marketing Quickstart | Free Guide + Workbook" description="Start building the next freelance opportunity before the current work runs out with the free Developer Marketing Quickstart guide and workbook." enableCheckoutOverlay={commerce.purchasable}>
  <PageHero
    image={heroImage}
    imageAlt="Dark developer workspace at night with warm desk lighting and city lights beyond the window"
    eyebrow="Free · Developer Marketing Quickstart"
    title="Start building the next opportunity before the current work runs out."
    description="Put one real acquisition loop into motion: choose a buyer, investigate a problem, shape a provisional offer, choose one channel, qualify a First 25, work the cycle, and use what happens to decide what to test next."
    audience={d.audience}
    supportingItems={["Free", "64-page guide", "45-page workbook", "Email required"]}
  >
    <div slot="actions"><ProductCTA product={product} location="free-hero" /></div>
    <div slot="visual" class="gold-glow min-w-0 max-w-full overflow-hidden"><ProductCover product={product} /></div>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="px-4 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8"><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[.72fr_1.28fr] lg:gap-20"><div><p class="editorial-kicker">The moment acquisition usually starts too late</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The current project is almost over, so the next client search suddenly becomes urgent.</h2></div><div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground"><p>When acquisition only gets attention after delivery slows down, the business starts the next search under pressure. That can make a weak prospect look more attractive, make pricing harder to hold, and turn the first available opportunity into the one that has to work.</p><p>The Quickstart gives future work calendar space before the current project is finished.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="border-y border-border bg-card/35 px-4 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl"><div class="max-w-3xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Build a first cycle you can learn from</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Give the market something specific enough to answer.</h2><p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">The first cycle does not need to be perfect. It needs to be concrete enough that buyer behavior can teach you something about the market, problem, offer, message, channel, and prospect selection.</p></div><ol class="mt-10 grid gap-px overflow-hidden border border-border bg-border md:grid-cols-2">{steps.map(([title, body], index) => <li class="bg-background p-7"><p class="font-mono text-xs text-primary-accent">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</p><h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold">{title}</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">{body}</p></li>)}</ol></div></section>

  <section class="px-4 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8"><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[.72fr_1.28fr] lg:gap-20"><div><p class="editorial-kicker">What you know after the first cycle</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The useful result is a better next decision.</h2></div><div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground"><p>You may learn that the market is reachable but the problem is weak. The problem may be credible but the offer may need to change. The offer may be sound but the wrong stakeholder is being contacted. The channel may be a poor fit. The list may be weak. The message may be unclear.</p><p>The cycle gives those possibilities evidence. That is more useful than changing everything because the first batch did not produce the result you hoped for.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="border-y border-border bg-card/35 px-4 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8"><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20"><div><p class="editorial-kicker">When you need a deeper acquisition operating system</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Client Acquisition Without Upwork</h2><p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Go deeper into account selection, research, outreach, follow-up, nurture, qualification, pipeline states, measurement, channel economics, capacity, and diagnosis.</p><p class="mt-6"><a class="font-semibold text-primary-accent hover:underline" href="/products/client-acquisition-without-upwork/">Explore Client Acquisition Without Upwork →</a></p></div><div><p class="editorial-kicker">When the broader problem is market understanding</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Marketing for Builders</h2><p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Go deeper into positioning, buyer meaning, proof, buyer-facing infrastructure, market access, activation, diagnosis, and marketing management.</p><p class="mt-6"><a class="font-semibold text-primary-accent hover:underline" href="/products/marketing-for-builders/">Explore Marketing for Builders →</a></p></div></div></section>

  <section class="px-4 py-18 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8"><div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Questions before you download</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Use the free product for the first live acquisition loop.</h2><div class="mt-8"><FAQList faqs={faqs} /></div><div class="mt-12 border-t border-border pt-10"><h2 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Give the next client search a head start.</h2><p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">Choose a buyer, investigate a problem, build a provisional offer, qualify a First 25, work the cycle, and learn from what happens before the current project leaves you searching under pressure.</p><div class="mt-8"><ProductCTA product={product} location="free-final" /></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
